id: 24
hanzi: 谣言
pinyin: yáo yán
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Noun

meanings_summary:
  en: rumor; unfounded story; gossip; falsehood
  es: rumor; bulo; patraña; falsedad infundada

senses[1]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Noun | Standard | a fabricated, unverified, or groundless statement or report circulating among people without factual basis | noticia falsa, invención o testimonio carente de base real que se propaga entre el público | 制造谣言 (fabricate rumors)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 赵王缺乏政治鉴别力，轻信了秦国散布的虚假谣言，错误地罢免了前线坚守的老将廉颇。 | Zhàowáng quēfá zhèngzhì jiànbiélì, qīngxìn le Qínguó sànbù de xūjiǎ yáoyán, cuòwù de bàmǐan le qiánxiàn jiānshǒu de lǎojiàng Lián Pō. | Lacking political discernment, King Zhao gullibly believed the false rumors spread by Qin, mistakenly dismissing General Lian Po from the front. | Carente de lucidez política, el rey de Zhao creyó los falsos bulos difundidos por Qin y destituyó erróneamente al veterano Lian Po del frente.
  #2 | 公安网监部门及时发布权威通报澄清事实，迅速平息了在社交网络上引发恐慌的网络谣言。 | Gōng'ān wǎngjiān bùmén jíshí fābù quánwēi tōngbào chéngqīng shìshí, xùnsù píngxī le zài shèjiāo wǎngluò shang yǐnfā kǒnghuāng de wǎngluò yáoyán. | Cyber police promptly issued an authoritative bulletin clarifying the facts, swiftly quelling online rumors that had triggered public panic. | La policía cibernética emitió una nota oficial aclarando los hechos y disipando el pánico causado por bulos en redes sociales.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  制造谣言 | fabricate / concoct rumors
  散布谣言 | spread rumors
  谣言止于智者 | rumors stop with the wise
  辟谣澄清 | refute rumors and clarify
  网络谣言 | internet rumors / disinformation
  恶毒谣言 | malicious / venomous rumors

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  造谣生事 | zào yáo shēng shì | concoct rumors to stir up trouble
  满城风雨 | mǎn chéng fēng yǔ | the whole town is rife with gossip and talk
  三人成虎 | sān rén chéng hǔ | three people repeating a lie make a tiger; falsehood repeated sounds true
  杯弓蛇影 | bēi gōng shé yǐng | mistake the reflection of a bow for a snake; illusory panic

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  谣 | yáo | ballad; folk rhyme; rumor; fabricate | balada; copla popular; rumor; bulo | 讠 | speech | 讠 (spoken speech) + 䍃 (earthenware jar / floating ballad) | 䍃 (yáo) | 12 | 左右结构 | Spoken street verses 讠 sung without instrumental accompaniment like jars 䍃; evolved into circulating hearsay. | Words of speech (讠) drifting through streets like singing ballads, mutating into unverified hearsay (谣). | Palabras orales (讠) que vuelan por las calles como coplas anónimas mutando en habladurías (谣). | 35 | IVBOU | 謠
  言 | yán | words; speech; talk; say | palabra; lenguaje; hablar; discurso | 言 | speech | tongue emitting breath strokes 口 from mouth | 言 (yán) | 7 | 单一结构 | Ancient pictograph of sound strokes radiating upward from an open human mouth 口; signifies speech. | Articulate sound waves radiating upward from an open mouth (口) as spoken words (言). | Ondas sonoras que brotan de la boca abierta (口) articulando palabras humanas (言). | 35 | YMR | 言

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: Fabricated street ballads (谣) uttered as spoken words (言) constitute unfounded rumors (谣言).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Coplas anónimas de callejuela (谣) formuladas en lenguaje hablado (言) conforman el bulo o rumor (谣言).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: Derived from classical street ballads (童谣) that carried political prophecies or weaponized counter-intelligence.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Double second tone: 'yáo yán' (35-35). Rise cleanly on both syllables with steady cadence.

traps_and_cognates:
  look_alikes[4]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,distinction_note}:
    摇 | yáo | shake; rock | Hand radical 扌 on left instead of 讠
    遥 | yáo | distant; remote | Movement 辶 around 䍃 instead of 讠
    信 | xìn | letter; believe | Person 亻 on left of 言
    誓 | shì | swear; vow | Fold 折 on top of 言
  etymological_cognates[4]{character,pinyin,gloss_en}:
    歌谣 | gēyáo | ballad; folk song
    民谣 | mínyáo | folk ballad
    言语 | yányǔ | speech; spoken words
    言论 | yánlùn | discourse; speech

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 谣言 specifically designates unfounded, fabricated, and maliciously circulated falsehoods.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 谣言 vs. 真相 | zhēnxiàng | 真相 is the direct antonym meaning objective facts and verified truth.
    2 | 谣言 vs. 谎言 | huǎngyán | 谎言 is a deliberate lie told by an individual, while 谣言 is an unverified story circulating across an entire community.
    3 | 谣言 vs. 传言 | chuányán | 传言 is a neutral term for circulating hearsay, whereas 谣言 strongly implies malicious fabrication.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | “三人成虎，积羽沉舟。”春秋战国时期的谋士们最擅长利用谣言实施心理战。秦国仅用数千金在邯郸散布谣言，便让多疑的赵王自毁长城，换下身经百战的廉颇。这表明心智不坚者面对谣言极易丧失理智判断。 | 'Sān rén chéng hǔ, jī yǔ chén zhōu.' Chūnqiū-Zhànguó shíqī de móushì men zuì shàncháng lìyòng yáoyán shíshī xīnlǐzhàn. Qínguó jǐn yòng shù qiān jīn zài Hándān sànbù yáoyán, biàn ràng duōyí de Zhàowáng zìhuǐ-chángchéng, huàn xià shēnjīng-bǎizhàn de Lián Pō. Zhè biǎomíng xīnji bù jiān zhě miànduì yáoyán jí yì sàngshī lǐzhì pànduàn. | 'Three men make a tiger; piled feathers sink a ship.' Sages excelled at weaponizing rumors in psychological warfare. A few thousand pieces of gold spreading rumors in Handan tricked King Zhao into firing Lian Po, destroying his realm. | 'Tres voces inventan un tigre; plumas amontonadas hunden un bajel.' Los estrategas antiguos dominaban la guerra psicológica con bulos. Con poco oro esparcido en Handan, Qin empujó al monarca de Zhao a relevar al curtido Lian Po.
  #2 | 古人云：“谣言止于智者。”在信息传播极为迅捷的今天，面对网络上真伪难辨的各种传言，保持清醒的理性头脑尤为珍贵。不信谣、不传谣，主动探寻权威证据，才是每一个具有独立思考能力的公民应当具备的素养。 | Gǔrén yún: 'Yáoyán zhǐ yú zhìzhě.' Zài xìnxī chuánbō jíwéi xùnjié de jīntiān, miànduì wǎngluò shang zhēnwěi-nánbiàn de gè zhǒng chuányán, bǎochí qīngxǐng de lǐxìng tóunǎo yóuwéi zhēnguì. Bù xìnyáo, bù chuányáo, zhǔdòng tànxún quánwēi zhèngjù, cái shì měi yī gè jùyǒu dúlì sīkǎo nénglì de gōngmín yīngdāng jùbèi de sùyǎng. | As ancients said: 'Rumors stop with the wise.' Today, facing hard-to-verify gossip on networks, maintaining a cool, rational mind is precious. Refusing to believe or spread rumors and seeking authority reflects critical citizenship. | Como sentenciaron los clásicos: 'El rumor cesa ante el sabio.' En la sociedad digital, preservar la cabeza fría ante noticias confusas es virtud suprema. Rechazar bulos y buscar fuentes fidedignas es el sello del ciudadano libre.
